WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.360
What do you call a sleeping bull?

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.720
A bull dozer!

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.660
Imagine you wake up from your sleep one night

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.620
to find that someone is trying to harm you.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.900
You try moving your hands and legs

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.680
but you cannot move a single muscle in your body!

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.700
Even your voice seems choked. You feel helpless!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:29.140
Did you know that such situations are really experienced by people?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.980
Why does this happen?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.800
Let's find out!

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.580
There is a scientific reason behind this.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.260
This could be due to a Sleep disorder called Sleep Paralysis.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.500
This strange phenomenon can occur

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.360
at two different moments while sleeping.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.800
One is when we are just falling asleep.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.440
And second during one of the stages of our sleep cycle

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.920
called the Rapid eye movement.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.940
Let's talk about the second case,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.980
which is more serious than the first.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.620
We know that we go through two major stages during our sleep cycle.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.140
One is the Non-rapid eye movement sleep,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.660
which itself is subdivided into four stages.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.100
And the second is the Rapid eye movement sleep.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.940
NREM sleep in general is a dreamless sleep.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.120
And these stages are the ones, which lead into the rapid eye movement

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.360
or REM.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.240
Now during REM sleep

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.420
the brain is very active.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.120
It is in this stage that we have vivid dreams.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.740
Another characteristic of the stage is that

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.520
the muscles of the body are essentially turned off.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.160
This is done by our brain,

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.560
to avoid hurting ourselves or others during dreams.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.960
Now what if a person suddenly wakes up

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.000
before the completion of the REM stage?

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:55.900
Sometimes in such a case

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.400
the mind is alert with eyes wide open,

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.340
but the muscles don't function!

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.860
That is the body cannot move

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.440
even as dreams continue to play inside the head.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:13.340
Hence, the person experiences auditory and sensory hallucinations.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.880
Scary right !

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.540
It is believed that four in ten people

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.600
experience this condition at least once in their lifetime.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.300
But for some,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.620
unfortunately, it occurs frequently.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.100
Well... now you might remember this video

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.620
if you ever have Sleep Paralysis.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.920
We saw how Sleep Paralysis can occur while we are in REM sleep!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.180
During this stage,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.760
our brain shuts down the muscle movements while we are dreaming.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.860
But now consider this interesting possibility.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.240
What if the opposite happens?

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.000
That is, we are in the REM sleep,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.640
we are dreaming, but our brain fails to shut down our muscle movement.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.560
What will happen in such a case?

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.260
Is such a condition even possible?

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.540
Well, this is your Kyu Box to explore.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.880
Let us know your findings in the comment section.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.060
